i want to create a bot for slack which will do the following: 1. listen for 
events corresponding to me publishing messages to channels. 2. rewrite my 
original text to make it more professional and friendly. The re-written text 
should be concise (no long prose and circular statements) while retaining the 
original semantic meaning and implications. 3. edit the original message with 
the new re-written text. edited messages should be signed off 'edited by 
xxx-bot' or something similar.

architecture wise, i expect the app to function as a server which listens for 
slack events via slacks app socket api. the event will serve as the trigger. 
upon triggering, the server should pull thread history as additional context via
api, followed by the actual re-writing step. i imagine the re-writes to be 
performed by an LLM, so the rewriting context and original text should be 
formatted into a prompt which is sent to the designed openai endpoint. the user 
shuold be free to designate any endpoint and key as any one of environment 
variable / yaml config / server launch input argument. Finally, there should be 
a post-processing step which checks for semantic similarity, tonal suitability, 
and conciseness of the re-written text. upon metric quality failure, there 
should be fallbacks to further refine the re-writes or do nothing to modify the 
text and log a silent error instead. Note that NOT doing any modificaiton is 
also a valid option if the original text already meets tonal and semantic 
requirements.
